From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: an activeTab grant reaches the tab before the click
 does

ActiveTabPermissionGranter told the tab's renderer about a grant only in
NotifyGranted, after a round trip to the network service for the
extension's CORS allowlist. The tray grants and then dispatches
action.onClicked at once, as ExtensionActionRunner::RunAction does, so a
listener's scripting.executeScript could reach the tab ahead of the grant
and be refused: "Cannot access contents of the page".
guard-webview-active-tab.sh failed that way 7 ms after the click.

GrantIfRequested now sends the tab's process its new permissions itself,
before returning. The tab needs no allowlist, and the message goes over
the channel any later ExecuteCode does, so it arrives first.
NotifyGranted is unchanged and sends it again.
---
 .../permissions/active_tab_permission_granter.cc | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/extensions/browser/permissions/active_tab_permission_granter.cc b/extensions/browser/permissions/active_tab_permission_granter.cc
index 37bd0fc5f3..80df21bcc2 100644
--- a/extensions/browser/permissions/active_tab_permission_granter.cc
+++ b/extensions/browser/permissions/active_tab_permission_granter.cc
@@ -188,6 +188,22 @@ void ActiveTabPermissionGranter::GrantIfRequested(const Extension* extension) {
                                   new_hosts.Clone(), new_hosts.Clone());
     permissions_data->UpdateTabSpecificPermissions(tab_id_, new_permissions);
 
+    // Domicile's engine fork: the tab's own renderer is told now, not after
+    // the network service has the new CORS allowlist. NotifyGranted waits for
+    // that round trip, and a caller that dispatches action.onClicked straight
+    // after granting -- ExtensionActionRunner::RunAction, and Domicile's tray
+    // -- has the listener's scripting.executeScript reach the tab first and be
+    // refused. The tab's process needs no allowlist, and this goes over the
+    // same channel as any ExecuteCode sent after it, so it arrives first.
+    // NotifyGranted still sends it again, with the extension processes'.
+    content::RenderProcessHost* tab_process =
+        web_contents()->GetPrimaryMainFrame()->GetProcess();
+    ScriptInjectionTracker::WillGrantActiveTab(
+        base::PassKey<ActiveTabPermissionGranter>(), *extension, *tab_process);
+    UpdateTabSpecificPermissions(extension->id(), new_hosts, tab_id_,
+                                 /*update_origin_allowlist=*/false,
+                                 tab_process);
+
     SetCorsOriginAccessList(
         browser_context, *extension,
         base::BindOnce(&ActiveTabPermissionGranter::NotifyGranted,
